{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e","id":1335355,"title":"In Which Alucard Discusses Personas... (Exalted 3e)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-12T15:19:29-07:00","id":1335355,"title":"In Which Alucard Discusses Personas... (Exalted 3e)","content":"Because <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1335231#post1335231\">someone in Ask a Question, Get an Answer</a> asked for a guide to the persona Charms in Socialize, I thought I'd take a moment to expand on my experience with the Charms.<br /> <br /> <b>First Impressions</b><br /> <br /> I'll be honest - my very first read of the book, I was a bit confused when I got to Socialize. I asked myself, &quot;Why would I take these? If I want to be someone else, that's what Larceny is for, isn't it?&quot; Of course, this was before I had fully internalized the new social system, before I'd realized how key the presence or absence of Intimacies were. I came to realize that having access to an entirely different set of Intimacies wouldn't just make it harder to read my true intentions - while assuming a persona, my real Intimacies are effectively invulnerable.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, it takes a very weird sort of person to <i>want</i> to do that, right?<br /> <br /> \u200bThe progression of Charms seemed to follow a sort of logic, at least - some folks claimed it came out of nowhere, but to me it seemed pretty straightforward: you start out with having a good poker face, advance to being able to indefinitely keep your intentions hidden, move on to hiding a specific thing you care about, to making it seem like you care about it in an <i>entirely</i> different context, to having an entirely different set of Intimacies, et cetera.<br /> <br /> I put aside the Socialize rules and didn't think much on them as I ran my first Exalted 3e game, since it was a seafaring game and the PCs were largely interested in treasures and gods and monsters. I would occasionally call for a Read Intentions roll, but even the PCs who put dots in Socialize didn't purchase any of its Charms, so at the time it was largely just there for the PCs to find the leverage for their massive Presence pools.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspirational Material</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAs the game went on, I got the itch to play Ex3 without having to sit in the ST chair. As my seafaring game's players dropped off one by one to RL concerns, I began to wonder about PCs I could make for the time when I would eventually take a turn at playing.<br /> <br /> That's when I started reading <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/doom-and-gloam\u200b\" target=\"_blank\">Doom and Gloam</a>, a campaign log of an Exalted 3e game in which Jenna Moran played Dessa Svetlana or Tepet Evdeniya, depending on whether she had her Socialize Charms active or not. Svetlana was a Socialize Supernal Night who had stepped into the identity of a missing Realm magistrate.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd also started rereading the Caste Books from Exalted 1e. By the time I read <i>Caste Book: Eclipse</i>, I was starting to see the appeal of a Socialize Solar.<br /> <br /> <b>Na na na na na na na na na na na na na, Batman!</b><br /> <br /> Some friends eventually announced games, and I made characters for them, but most of those have either fallen apart or been put on hold. Still, looking for a spot for Sundays, I found a Discord group that had an opening. Feeling a bit of whimsy, I decided to try a concept that was a little out-there (hey, one of the other PCs was named &quot;Invisible Horse Princess&quot;). I recalled a post of mine, from years ago, in which I'd asserted that any Caste of Solar could be played as Batman (given how many hats he wears, the numerous writers who've each had their own takes on him, and so on), and decided to put my money where my mouth was.<br /> <br /> \u200bI decided on an Eclipse Caste, asking myself, &quot;What if Batman had to <i>invent</i> Bruce Wayne?&quot;, and thus Knight Raiton was born.<br /> <br /> (Admittedly he's also got a bit of <i>Moon Knight</i> to him.)<br /> <br /> Knight Raiton is a masked vigilante detective who stalks the streets of Nexus by night. By day he lives as Carter Brus, an affluent Guild factor residing in a mansion in the Bastion district with his manservant, Avery. Knight Raiton Exalted as an Eclipse Caste after capturing a murderer and bringing him to the family of his victim, and convincing them not to kill him.<br /> <br /> At character creation, I only went as deep as Heart-Eclipsing Shroud (because let's face it, if you're gonna be Batman, you're gonna want to be able to throw a punch, solve a mystery, scare bad guys, throw a funny-shaped boomerang, and sneak around), but since then I've expanded his Socialize milieu pretty drastically.<br /> <br /> \u200bKnight Raiton's Intimacies included a Defining pledge to never set aside his crusade, a Major contempt for murderers, a Major fondness for his friend and manservant, a Major mourning over his parents, and a Major promise to not become like the monsters he fights. On the other hand, his Intimacies as Carter included a Defining desire to live lavishly, a Major desire to protect his family's legacy, a Major fondness for his friend and manservant, and a Minor pleasure found in helping the needy.<br /> <br /> Overall, he\u2019s been a fun character to play, and the other players seem to enjoy how he holds animosity for the assassin PC, Invisible Horse Princess, in one moment, yet at other times seems to show respect for the heights to which she\u2019s bootstrapped herself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-21-2019, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T16:37:48-07:00","id":1335370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amdramnar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1335231#post1335231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am interested in a basic understanding of the charms, their interactions, and a good starting character designs.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, let's talk about the Charms.<br /> <br /> <b>The Persona Tree</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u200b<b>Heart-Eclipsing Shr-</b> Hey, hey, wait, hold it. The tree doesn't <i>start</i> with Heart-Eclipsing Shroud. It starts with Shadow Over Day.<br /> <br /> \u200bLet's try that again.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Over Day</b><br /> <br /> That's better. The road to personas starts with the ability to conceal your true intentions, and <i>that </i>starts with having a good Guile. Shadow Over Day gets the same effect as the Socialize Excellency, at half the cost. It's not a bad Charm, especially if you took Socialize as your Supernal or have Essence 2 for the ability to double up on it.<br /> <br /> <b>Guarded Thoughts Meditation</b><br /> <br /> \u200bOf course, even Shadow Over Day has trouble looking good next to the sheer magnificence of Guarded Thoughts Meditation's offer of an <i>Indefinite </i>+3 Guile for 4m. Sure, it's Simple to activate, but why would you not already have it active? Fact is, I've never uncommitted these motes as Knight Raiton. Between a good Manipulation+Socialize pool, this Charm, Shadow Over Day, and an applicable Specialty, you can get a Guile of <i>11</i> before you even factor in a stunt.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Penumbra Self Meditation</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAnother Simple Charm; if you suspect someone's going to have a problem with one of your Intimacies, you can spend an hour and pay 3m to make it effectively disappear. If Knight Raiton is going to masquerade as common criminal Wick Warrens to plant ideas in the head of T\u00e1ng L\u00e1ng, he's going to hide his hatred of murderers. After all, though his Guile is nearly invulnerable, Charms like Cunning Insight Technique allow for the possibility of discerning Intimacies <i>without checking against Guile</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Inverted Ego Mask</b><br /> <br /> \u200bA Reflexive Charm, Inverted Ego Mask lets you respond to someone piercing your Guile by changing the context of the Intimacy they perceive. Let's say T\u00e1ng L\u00e1ng's player rolls absolutely amazingly, taking Knight Raiton by surprise with fourteen successes on ten dice, and asks me if &quot;Wick Warrens&quot; has any Intimacies for his parents. I can activate Inverted Ego Mask, and they come away thinking that our disguised hero <i>hates</i> them.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart-Eclipsing Shroud</b><br /> <br /> \u200bFinally! Now you can spend ten motes and a Willpower over a four-hour period to not only hide your Intimacies, but to generate a set of false ones over them that make you effectively a different person. Here, you can lie so well that <i>you can become lost in it</i>. Remember that the persona created by Heart-Eclipsing Shroud needs the same number of Principles as the real you (but you can have as many or as few Ties as you want). When Knight Raiton took Heart-Eclipsing Shroud, I picked the character concept of &quot;wealthy playboy socialite.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> At this stage, the only difference between the character and his persona is his Intimacies. If you don't plan to go any further, you could even keep all the relevant details on one character sheet.<br /> <br /> <b>Hundred-Faced Stranger</b><br /> <br /> This is the one that gives your persona its own XP track; have a second sheet ready if you want this Charm. If you\u2019re interested in going this far, you\u2019ll pick an entire suite of Favored Abilities for the new you, with your pool of starting dots based on your investment in certain skills, and fill it out with half your character\u2019s XP.<br /> <br /> When I purchased this, I decided Carter Brus would be more reflective of a persuasive playboy with a head for business. He got dots in Integrity, Bureaucracy, and Presence (and Socialize of course).<br /> <br /> Just remember, certain skills like the Dawn Abilities, Craft, Lore, and Occult are capped by the ranking the real you possesses.<br /> <br /> (That said, Vance has said it\u2019s plenty reasonable for a persona for a martial artist to practice a different martial art from its initiate.)<br /> <br /> Your persona doesn\u2019t get his own Charms yet, but he can use any of <i>yours</i> that his Ability ratings qualify him for. Make sure you give your persona Socialize 5 so you can revert back when necessary!<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t spend <i>all</i> that XP on Abilities right away, though - if you\u2019re going this far, you might as well pick up\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Legend Mask Methodology</b><br /> <br /> Now your persona can qualify for its own Solar Charm purchases! For Carter, I used this chance to expand his Socialize and Bureaucracy repertoire even further, allowing him to shmooze his way to the top of Nexus\u2019 social circles (as well as get an audience with Shalrina, Daimyo of Faces).<br /> <br /> <b>Draw the Curtain</b><br /> <br /> This Charm increases the rate at which one of your personas accrues XP. One part says three-quarters, but the later part says two-thirds; I\u2019d recommend asking your ST to have it just be one or the other to avoid headache-inducing math.<br /> <br /> However, this Charm comes at the cost of a new Limit Trigger condition when you\u2019re in the persona for which you\u2019ve bought the Charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Fugue-Empowered Other</b><br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t got this Charm yet so I can\u2019t speak for its efficacy, but the basics of it is that you can borrow one of your persona\u2019s Abilities and the associated Charms for a single tick. However, use with care, as it brings with it the possibility of confusing your identities.<br /> <br /> <b>Soul Reprisal</b><br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t taken this one yet, nor do I think I will, but the long and short of it is, when you die, you can shed everything that was <i>you</i>, and continue to live as one of your personas. Better than just dying, I\u2019ll admit, but I\u2019m still not too keen on it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Complementary Charms</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">These aren\u2019t directly part of the same tree as Heart-Eclipsing Shroud, but you\u2019ll find they can expand your options and enhance your experience.<br /> <br /> (Assume all Charms are in Socialize unless otherwise noted!)<br /> <br /> <b>Easily-Discarded Presence Method</b><br /> <br /> If someone fails to penetrate your Guile, you can essentially force a would-be scrutinizer to disregard you entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Selfsame Master Procurer</b><br /> <br /> Essentially the opposite of Easily-Discarded Presence Method, if someone fails to penetrate your Guile, you become the object of their desires, the means by which they might accomplish their goal in this scene. (Be cautious about using this on someone if you haven\u2019t read <i>their</i> intentions yet!)<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Soul Void Kata</b><br /> <br /> \u200bIf someone fails to penetrate your Guile, you hypnotize them in such a way that they just stand there and can take no more actions for the rest of the scene. Hilarious, but I think I'll pass for now.<br /> <br /> <b>Preeminent Gala Knife</b><br /> <br /> Get motes back from Socialize actions? Yes, please! This makes those activations of Shadow Over Day more than worth it!<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Undying Solar Resolve (Integrity)</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThis Charm <i>also</i> refuels your mote pool, this time when someone tries to influence, curse, or mind-control you and rolls 1s or 2s.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Seasoned Criminal Method (Larceny)</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThis Charm grants you a suite of facades to adopt, which can be layered over your personas to make them even more varied. Knight Raiton can emanate Dissonance to make it harder to investigate his secret identity, while Carter Brus can appear to be a hapless mark when finding himself in a shadier part of Nexus. (The effective Intimacy from the Familiarity option is also invaluable!)<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise (Larceny)</b><br /> <br /> \u200bIf you really want to sell the idea that Knight Raiton is not Carter Brus and vice-versa, it helps to have them not <i>both</i> look like handsome, square-jawed, dark-haired athletic-types.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Perfect Mirror (Larceny)</b><br /> <br /> \u200bIf both you and your persona are known as Exalts, it helps to make it appear as though their animas are different as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Master Thespian Style (Performance)</b><br /> <br /> The poor man's Heart-Eclipsing Shroud. \u200bA scene-length one-point Guile booster, which only costs one mote. If someone fails to penetrate your Guile while you're in-character, they assume you have Intimacies in keeping with the role you're playing.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-21-2019, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T18:26:05-07:00","id":1335383,"title":"","content":"Thanks, by the way to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/322-madletter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar322_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"322\" data-vbnamecard=\"322\">MadLetter</a> for your Charm cascade PDFs. <a href=\"http://www.madletter.net/rpg/exalted/cascades/v2/cascade_v2_socialize.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">The Socialize cascade</a> in particular has been invaluable for organizing my thoughts!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T19:03:31-07:00","id":1335387,"title":"","content":"And reading on this tree and the personas is making me imagine the incredibly weird idea of all sample Nights in the castebook actually being Ravesh the Vanisher (or whoever you want to be the &quot;core&quot;).... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T19:14:26-07:00","id":1335390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335387#post1335387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And reading on this tree and the personas is making me imagine the incredibly weird idea of all sample Nights in the castebook actually being Ravesh the Vanisher (or whoever you want to be the &quot;core&quot;).... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m pretty sure it\u2019s \u201cHavesh the Vanisher,\u201d but nah, that wasn\u2019t really his M.O. - again, this isn\u2019t a disguise (though it doesn\u2019t hurt to look different between identities), so much as method-acting hard enough that you are effectively someone else.<br /> <br /> Mirror Flag\u2019s an Eclipse, not a Night, but she\u2019s a much better fit for the sort of mindset that leads to a character taking Heart-Eclipsing Shroud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T19:48:16-07:00","id":1335394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335390#post1335390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure it\u2019s \u201cHavesh the Vanisher,\u201d but nah, that wasn\u2019t really his M.O. - again, this isn\u2019t a disguise (though it doesn\u2019t hurt to look different between identities), so much as method-acting hard enough that you are effectively someone else.<br /> <br /> Mirror Flag\u2019s an Eclipse, not a Night, but she\u2019s a much better fit for the sort of mindset that leads to a character taking Heart-Eclipsing Shroud.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you're correct in both instances.<br /> But then finding out all other eclipses are actually Mirror Flag would probably generate more of a &quot;Should have known...&quot; than &quot;WHAT&quot; moment (Maybe it is the Emissary too, hiding in plain sight). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T20:36:21-07:00","id":1335408,"title":"","content":"This inspired me to go looking back at Lunar Guile Charms, and I'm blown away by how I completely missed (or could ever have forgotten about) Silver Mask Submersion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T21:07:54-07:00","id":1335411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335408#post1335408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This inspired me to go looking back at Lunar Guile Charms, and I'm blown away by how I completely missed (or could ever have forgotten about) Silver Mask Submersion.</div> </div> </div> </div> I plan to cover those at a later time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T03:05:39-07:00","id":1335444,"title":"","content":"This is a good guide. I think Batman (or other superheroes) are probably some of the best examples for Persona charms. Though I think for most characters, you can probably stop at Heart-Eclipsing Shroud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T03:11:35-07:00","id":1335449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335444#post1335444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I think for most characters, you can probably stop at Heart-Eclipsing Shroud.</div> </div> </div> </div>For most characters you can probably stop <i>before</i> Heart-Eclipsing Shroud. I\u2019m going to continue to expand on this once I get home from work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T04:14:11-07:00","id":1335454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your persona doesn\u2019t get his own Charms yet, but he can use any of <i>yours</i> that his Ability ratings qualify him for. Make sure you give your persona Socialize 5 so you can revert back when necessary! </div> </div> </div>Well that's really fun I never thought this could be a legit case. Had me laugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T05:05:11-07:00","id":1335461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335454#post1335454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's really fun I never thought this could be a legit case.</div> </div> </div> </div>That arguably happened with Batman of Zur-En-Arrh, in 2008.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T05:17:53-07:00","id":1335466,"title":"","content":"That's even funnier to see it actually happened in a Comics. Thanks for sharing this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T05:49:14-07:00","id":1335474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335461#post1335461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That arguably happened with Batman of Zur-En-Arrh, in 2008.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because everything is possible to Batman - including become <b>another</b> Batman <b><i>so hard</i></b> he forgets to revert back to Batman. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T06:48:35-07:00","id":1335486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335454#post1335454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's really fun I never thought this could be a legit case. Had me laugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes the challenge the Eclipse faces to survive is so great that it outweighs the risk of never remembering who they once were. Those Socialize dots are needed elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T07:44:55-07:00","id":1335500,"title":"","content":"Do you suppose there is room for a Solar Charm that lets you jump into a different persona when you use Battle-Fury Focus? Possibly also Ascendant Battle-Visage, and similar combat power-up Charms?<br /> <br /> Because I've always thought that Lunars had room for an upgrade to Dark Premise Duality, where activating Hybrid Body Transformation, Deadly Beastman Transformation, or Relentless Lunar Fury would allow the Lunar to instantly jump into (or out of) Shadow-Mind Meditation for the duration of the combat power-up Charm.<br /> <br /> Neither would let you change your combat Abilities, but you could gain other Charms potentially useful for combat. A Solar might cast aside his Performance Charms for terrifying Presence Charms, or his War Charms for leading men in exchange for Survival Charms for commanding his beast companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T08:29:14-07:00","id":1335514,"title":"","content":"<b>Other Splats</b><br /> <br /> Let's look at how other splats approach the idea of becoming someone else!<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Dragon-Blooded</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Terrestrial Exalted have a much more difficult time of compartmentalizing away their true selves. Still, it's startling what they can accomplish when they put their minds to it, and oftentimes in the Scarlet Dynasty, it's <i>necessary</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Loquacious Courtier Technique</b><br /> <br /> \u200bIt's the Socialize Excellency, what more do you expect? Actually, though, it's got the Mute keyword. Pretty nice, if you ask me.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Smoke-Wreathed Mien</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThis one lets you sabotage other people's Read Intentions rolls for 3m.<br /> <br /> <b>Watching the Salon's Shadows</b><br /> <br /> \u200bFew options exist to reduce or negate the penalty to your Guile for being unaware that you're under observation. Not only does Watching the Salon's Shadows boost your Guile against an unseen observer, it can grant you a roll to spot them, with double 9s.<br /> <br /> <b>Smoke Without Flame</b><br /> <br /> Another Guile-booster, if the observer fails to penetrate your Guile, you can exaggerate the intensity of your apparent emotions or the context of an Intimacy you possess; a repurchase allows you to perform this exaggeration even if they beat your Guile.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Ego-Dissolving Deception</b><br /> <br /> \u200bSpend an hour in meditation to rewrite one of your memories as a Psyche effect, drop the commitment to instantly restore your original memories. Very cool, much love.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Enticing Flame Feint</b><br /> <br /> \u200bProtect your allies from read intentions actions, at a cost of 1 point of Guile per use.<br /> <br /> <b>Implacable Dragon Mien</b><br /> <br /> \u200bA day-length Guile booster, this provides +2 Guile unless you want to hide a Major or Defining Intimacy based off an emotion; in Earth aura, it rises to +3 Guile, and even applies a +1 Guile for your emotion-based Intimacies.<br /> <br /> <b>Rippling Mirror Face</b><br /> <br /> \u200bWhen someone is trying to read your intentions and fails, you can show them an Intimacy you discovered in someone else via read intentions earlier in the scene<br /> <br /> (For your consideration, there's also <b>Wary Yellow Dog Attitude</b>, which lets you use your Socialize in place of Awareness for Join Battle. Doesn't directly hide your intentions, but if you're going this deep into Socialize you'll want this Charm. Also worth looking at is <b>Slippery Thoughts Technique</b> in Integrity, in which you can substitute your Manipulation for Wits in calculating your Resolve. <b>Pirate-Masquerading Method</b> in Sail is handy for blending in at a wretched hive of scum and villainy.)\u200b</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Lunars</b><br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Lunars are already good at <i>physically</i> becoming someone else, but what about when they want to blend in <i>socially</i>? Guile can be an important trait for a Lunar, as no matter how good your shapeshifting is, it's going to get awkward when you pose as an Immaculate and another monk uses Read Intentions to discern a Defining Tie of Reverence for Luna.<br /> <br /> <b>The Changing Moon Anima Power</b><br /> <br /> \u200bTechnically not a Charm, but it's an excellent start; if your anima is Dim, you get a constant +1 non-Charm bonus point of Guile. Very handy.<br /> <br /> <b>Lunar Excellency</b><br /> <br /> Solid enough on its own, but gets much better when you remember that you can add another Attribute to your dice cap with an appropriate stunt. So make sure and describe how only a hero of legendary stamina could hold up this fa\u00e7ade for so long, or how your quick thinking is all happening deep beneath the serene smiling surface, et cetera., and get those extra dice.<br /> <br /> \u200bUnless otherwise mentioned, assume the following Charms are in <i>Manipulation</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Moonlight Curtain Drawn</b><br /> <br /> \u200bScene-length +1 Guile; if defeating your Guile would reveal information inconsistent with your current shape, it increases to +3 Guile. Not bad for 3m. A repurchase lets you extend its duration to one day.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Cat-Eyed Enticement</b><br /> <br /> \u200bIf you successfully assert Guile against someone in a scene, you can use this Charm to reroll a number of failed dice to influence that person.<br /> <br /> <b>Argent Deceiver Smile</b><br /> <br /> Upgrades Moonlight Curtain Drawn - now if defeating your Guile would reveal you're trying to deceive someone, you can pay 2m to get the +3 Guile from Moonlight Curtain Drawn.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Seven-Veiled Visage</b><br /> <br /> \u200bFor one mote, (Essence) 1s on the opponent's roll to pierce your Guile subtract successes. If you're in a human shape the target has a Defining Intimacy towards, their failure to understand you throws them into despair, penalizing their social and mental dice pools for the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>\u200bSublime Fa\u00e7ade Art</b><br /> <br /> You can substitute in Integrity, Larceny, or Performance in place of Socialize to calculate Guile, and can pay one mote to remove a point of penalty from your Guile (though you can't reduce the penalty for being unaware of your observer).<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Anemones Conceal Clownfish</b><br /> <br /> \u200bBoost your buddy's Guile, boost how high he can raise his Guile, <i>and</i> if he's your Solar mate, any motes he spends on his Guile are muted.<br /> <br /> <b>Forgotten Self Wisdom</b><br /> <br /> \u200bPay 3m to suppress an Intimacy you have that's incompatible with a form you're shapeshifting into. Ends if you leave that form, and if you use the suppressed Intimacy to bolster Resolve or for a decision point, you can't use the Charm again for the rest of the day.<br /> <br /> <b>Labyrinth of the Beast</b><br /> <br /> Akin to the Solar Easily-Discarded Presence Method, if you successfully assert your Guile, and the person trying to read your intentions rolls at least one 1, they see only some animalistic drive (lust, hunger, et cetera.), and disregard you further. <i>If you're in an animal shape</i>, you can use it on even a successful read intentions (as long as they rolled at least one 1).<br /> <br /> <b>Inconspicuous Feral Lifestyle</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAs long as you're in an animal shape, acting like that animal, living the simple life of a beast, the cost of Labyrinth of the Beast falls to one mote, and can be used even against rolls with no 1s.<br /> <br /> <b>River Reflects Desire</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAfter you assert Guile against a roll with at least one 1, the person trying to read you sees what they <i>want</i> to see, as opposed to the truth.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Silver Mask Submersion</b><br /> <br /> \u200bUsed when you assume the shape of a human to whom you possess an Intimacy, or an animal, you overwrite your personality with that of the shape into which you are sliding. You replace your Intimacies with those of the form you're taking (or a set appropriate to representing the animal's instincts), and repress any memories incompatible with your new identity. Now unaware of your shapeshifter nature, you can't voluntarily leave this form (though you still have full access to your Charms) until the story ends, though you can set conditions for the Charm to come to an end (such as a certain phrase being said, a character dying, or a certain amount of time passing).<br /> <br /> <b>Will-Drowning Void</b><br /> <br /> Spend 6m to steal a Willpower from someone who fails to penetrate your Guile.<br /> <br /> <b>Mind-Shattering Mystery</b><br /> <br /> Spend \u200b7m, 1 wp to roll to afflict a target who failed to penetrate your Guile with madness.<br /> \u200b<br /> Also worth considering:<br /> <br /> <b>Inexplicable Mystery Incarnation</b><br /> <br /> \u200bMute the motes you spend on increasing Guile, social influence, or read intentions, for 2m.<br /> <br /> <b>Lying to the World</b><br /> <br /> Regain two motes when you successfully assert your Guile.<br /> <br /> <b>Whispering Silver Serpent</b><br /> <br /> \u200bSupplement a lie with this Charm, and for the rest of the scene, it can't be uncovered with Read Intentions or Profile Character actions.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Appearance: Mysterious Stranger Intimation</b><br /> <br /> \u200b+1 Guile against characters affected by Alluring Scent Technique.<br /> <br /> <b>Intelligence: Crossroads Walker Entreaty</b><br /> <br /> \u200b+1 Resolve and Guile against spirits and fae, and moreover, bars them from attacking you as long as you and your buddies don't attack or piss them off.<br /> <br /> <b>Wits: Shadow Mind Meditation</b><br /> <br /> \u200bSpend ten motes to and a Willpower to give yourself a &quot;shadow-mind&quot; that shares your Defining Intimacies (and your Intimacy for your Solar mate), but is only permitted negative Minor and Major Intimacies (nor is it permitted to voluntarily form them). Four hours of meditation lets you switch or from to the shadow-mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Wits: Dark Premise Duality</b><br /> <br /> \u200bYour shadow-mind can have different mental and social Attributes from you.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-16-2019, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T08:41:54-07:00","id":1335518,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Wary Yellow Dog Attitude is a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T09:43:52-07:00","id":1335532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335500#post1335500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you suppose there is room for a Solar Charm that lets you jump into a different persona when you use Battle-Fury Focus? Possibly also Ascendant Battle-Visage, and similar combat power-up Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hypothetically possible, but considering that personas don't have different Abilities by default (plus the restriction against putting more Dawn dots into a persona than you yourself have), it seems rather niche.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335500#post1335500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I've always thought that Lunars had room for an upgrade to Dark Premise Duality, where activating Hybrid Body Transformation, Deadly Beastman Transformation, or Relentless Lunar Fury would allow the Lunar to instantly jump into (or out of) Shadow-Mind Meditation for the duration of the combat power-up Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to review the Lunar Charms again, but I think this is one of those that could fit Lunars better. But first, bed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T10:14:25-07:00","id":1335542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335532#post1335532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hypothetically possible, but considering that personas don't have different Abilities by default (plus the restriction against putting more Dawn dots into a persona than you yourself have), it seems rather niche.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335500#post1335500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither would let you change your combat Abilities, but you could gain other Charms potentially useful for combat. A Solar might cast aside his Performance Charms for terrifying Presence Charms, or his War Charms for leading men in exchange for Survival Charms for commanding his beast companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you exchange Stealth Charms for Presence Charms? Bureaucracy Charms for Integrity or Awareness Charms?<br /> <br /> I'm away from my books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T17:12:21-07:00","id":1335629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335542#post1335542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you exchange Stealth Charms for Presence Charms? Bureaucracy Charms for Integrity or Awareness Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don\u2019t \u201cexchange Charms.\u201d Your persona has the same Charms as you.<br /> <br /> (Though the purchase of Hundred-Faced Stranger may cause it to no longer qualify if its Ability ratings don\u2019t meet the prereqs. Carter, for instance, has Dodge 1, where Knight Raiton has Dodge 4.)<br /> <br /> It won\u2019t have different Charms from you unless you\u2019ve gone as far as Legend Mask Methodology. But without Draw the Curtain, the persona only has half your XP (and <i>with</i> Draw the Curtain, somewhere between two-thirds and three-quarters your XP). <br /> <br /> Again, I didn\u2019t say no, I said it was hypothetically possible, but rather niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-13-2019, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T18:04:36-07:00","id":1335637,"title":"","content":"I think the strongest way to conceive of persona Charms is to question whether anybody here would recognise me if they met me in real life (having been informed ahead of time that it was me).<br /> <br /> We don't need disguises or alter egos to be different people in different scenarios. One way or another, different contexts can demand different forms of presentation or engagement.<br /> <br /> Solar magic merely heightens the reality of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T05:08:27-07:00","id":1335703,"title":"","content":"Do you have the same anima and stuff in your alternatives personas ? Does this break anything or are there any alternatives? I believe there is a larcin Charm that allows to change that. Would you recommend it to use with Personas ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T05:31:02-07:00","id":1335706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335703#post1335703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have the same anima and stuff in your alternatives personas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, your anima remains the same. That\u2019s why I mentioned Perfect Mirror in the complementary Charms section (though right now, no one but his fellow PCs know Carter Brus is a Solar).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335703#post1335703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this break anything or are there any alternatives?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not showing anima is an option that\u2019s worked out pretty well for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335703#post1335703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you recommend it to use with Personas ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t have listed it if I didn\u2019t think it was a good Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T06:19:32-07:00","id":1335715,"title":"","content":"Actually I think a charm to quickly swap personas is a boon for playing superheroes. Doesn't take Clark Kent four hours to become superman, does it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T07:18:54-07:00","id":1335719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335715#post1335715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I think a charm to quickly swap personas is a boon for playing superheroes. Doesn't take Clark Kent four hours to become superman, does it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I made it an Evocation for my suit of artifact armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T07:20:41-07:00","id":1335720,"title":"","content":"Ah, so you put it on and Raiton wakes up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T08:08:00-07:00","id":1335725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335720#post1335720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so you put it on and Raiton wakes up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Once I buy it, I can revert back to Raiton from a persona by donning the armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T10:13:42-07:00","id":1335742,"title":"","content":"When it comes to something like anima, I think that one's first approach to the persona Charms is not as a form of physical disguise, but about creating multiple configurations of your own personality for interacting with different groups.<br /> <br /> Consider a scenario in which you meet with various factions, openly under your own identity and without any modifications to your appearance, and they all get different reads on you and different qualities that they can successfully appeal to. Maybe they even know that you're in contact with other groups, but each persona claims that to the others it's all a double agent act, and their genuine loyalty is to your group. How can that be disproven?<br /> <br /> Or take away any form of dissembling at all. You become the monarch of a nation, and craft one persona for when meeting with the nobles, one for meeting with the civil service, one for the national diet, one for the common masses, and one for in private.<br /> <br /> Which face is the original one? Which is the real one? Does it even matter? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335715#post1335715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't take Clark Kent four hours to become superman, does it?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but their personalities are identical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T10:44:12-07:00","id":1335751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335742#post1335742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which face is the original one? Which is the real one? Does it even matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. Does it?<br /> <br /> You're a Solar heavily invested in social abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335742#post1335742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but their personalities are identical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Timid, bumbling, mild mannered Clark Kent has the same fearless, front-line personality as Superman.<br /> <br /> Kent, who faints and runs away from trouble to go get help, has the same apparent Intimacies as Superman?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T11:53:05-07:00","id":1335761,"title":"","content":"In many versions, Kent is a serious investigative journalist who doesn't let intimidation or corporate oversight stop from crusading for the truth. The public Bruce Wayne face is far more different to Batman than Clark Kent is to Superman. <br /> <br /> They do have different personalities, but not, I think, different intimacies. I don't think Superman is hiding his intimacies well as Clark Kent, he's hiding his personality. (So... a defence against a Profile Character action?)<br /> <br /> Still, 4 hours I think is a bit much. Not for Superman, because he's not using it, but for those who are. Alucard's evocation is a good way to solve that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-14-2019, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T03:50:26-07:00","id":1335860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335751#post1335751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Timid, bumbling, mild mannered Clark Kent has the same fearless, front-line personality as Superman.<br /> <br /> Kent, who faints and runs away from trouble to go get help, has the same apparent Intimacies as Superman?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure that in the very long history of Superman there has been at least one wrong-headed version in which Clark Kent habitually forgets that he's invulnerable when he's not dressed in that leotard, but it's not the typical or popularly recognised form of the character.<br /> <br /> So Clark Kent is not actually timid in the face of things that he knows can't hurt him, and when he runs away it's not because he's afraid but because he wants to get out of sight so that he can put on the leotard.<br /> <br /> One might note the Christopher Reeves movie, one of the most famous incarnations of the character, in which he artfully uses his phony bumbling as a way of throwing his invulnerable body in front of a bullet going for another person.<br /> <br /> Playing pretend when he's not wearing a costume is a bit different from genuine social adaptations.<br /> <br /> There's also those depictions of the character in which he acts a good deal more Superman when dressed as Clark, and a good deal more Clark when dressed as Superman, in the presence of people that are in on his secret.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think persona Charms aren't best suited to model superhero narratives, and that the emphasis on that or similar things is missing out on a lot of potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T05:33:13-07:00","id":1335868,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re not wrong, Isator; there\u2019s a lot of value in using these Charms (and their prereqs) to play the double-agent (hence why I\u2019m in the process of working up a second persona for Knight Raiton when I want to engage in shadier behavior).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-15-2019, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T07:45:25-07:00","id":1335888,"title":"","content":"I'm ambivalent about Lunar Shadow-Mind Meditation.<br /> <br /> It's like Solar Heart-Eclipsing Shroud, but you can only have one alternate persona, it's not even fully alternate since it must begin with the same Defining Intimacies and Tie for a Solar Mate, and it is always unrelentingly negative, bitter, cynical, skeptical, fearful, or hateful to the point that it cannot voluntarily cultivate a positive opinion.<br /> <br /> As a disguise against understanding and persuasion, it is lackluster.<br /> <br /> As a mental defense against seduction, the four hours needed to invoke it is really awkward.<br /> <br /> As a Hulk to your Bruce Banner (especially when using Dark Premise Duality with a theoretical upgrade so you can go DBT to immediately exchange your Intelligence for another dot in Wits and more Perception, and any dots in Manipulation for more in Charisma or Appearance) it takes a lot of investment for dubious returns outside of that specific application.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus, I was kind of hoping that a Lunar could craft alternative personae that took advantage of the fact that Lunar Exalted can have any of their potential Castes, by giving their personae a completely different Caste than theirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T09:12:13-07:00","id":1335906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335888#post1335888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm ambivalent about Lunar Shadow-Mind Meditation.<br /> <br /> It's like Solar Heart-Eclipsing Shroud, but you can only have one alternate persona, it's not even fully alternate since it must begin with the same Defining Intimacies and Tie for a Solar Mate, and it is always unrelentingly negative, bitter, cynical, skeptical, fearful, or hateful to the point that it cannot voluntarily cultivate a positive opinion.<br /> <br /> As a disguise against understanding and persuasion, it is lackluster.<br /> <br /> As a mental defense against seduction, the four hours needed to invoke it is really awkward.<br /> <br /> As a Hulk to your Bruce Banner (especially when using Dark Premise Duality with a theoretical upgrade so you can go DBT to immediately exchange your Intelligence for another dot in Wits and more Perception, and any dots in Manipulation for more in Charisma or Appearance) it takes a lot of investment for dubious returns outside of that specific application.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus, I was kind of hoping that a Lunar could craft alternative personae that took advantage of the fact that Lunar Exalted can have any of their potential Castes, by giving their personae a completely different Caste than theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way it's presented as the character's shadow self, I think its primary function is to bypass your own intimacies. Your shadow self is the cold-blooded realist inside you who goes behind your back and does all the dirty work it believes you're too soft or weak-willed to do yourself.<br /> <br /> Your shadow self will happily deal with the slaver you have a Major tie of Hatred towards, or abandon a friend if helping them would mean sacrificing something important to you. It doesn't bypass Defining Intimacies because you're both supposed to be trying to achieve the same thing in the end - what really changes is how you'll go about it and what you're willing to do to achieve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T09:28:32-07:00","id":1335909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335906#post1335906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your shadow self is the cold-blooded realist inside you who goes behind your back and does all the dirty work it believes you're too soft or weak-willed to do yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you're ALREADY a cold-blooded cynic more than willing to do dirty work? What good does it do you then?<br /> <br /> Do you then begin to spend most of your time in the shadow-mindset, treating it as your true self, and outside of that mind-set you begin to erode your negative Intimacies and cultivate more positive Intimacies in order to convince people whom you consider soft and weak-willed that you're one of them?<br /> <br /> <br /> Lunars are light as well as darkness. Is there no room for a Bright-Mind Meditation which makes it easier to reject negative influence and restricts you from forming such opinions voluntarily?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T09:54:40-07:00","id":1335912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335909#post1335909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you're ALREADY a cold-blooded cynic more than willing to do dirty work? What good does it do you then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things get a bit more complicated, but I guess you'd get something like an angry parent shadow self, someone who's mumbling to himself how he can't believe his true self is so conceited that he's forced to take over if they're going to do a good deed for no material reward. &quot;Do the right thing, you idiot!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335909#post1335909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are light as well as darkness. Is there no room for a Bright-Mind Meditation which makes it easier to reject negative influence and restricts you from forming such opinions voluntarily?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could ask Vance to be sure, but I think a Bright-Mind Meditation custom Charm fits in the Lunar design space and would be perfectly in-theme for a darker Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T16:00:13-07:00","id":1335955,"title":"","content":"I think if your lunar is already like that you... should take a different charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T16:29:44-07:00","id":1335961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335868#post1335868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You\u2019re not wrong, Isator; there\u2019s a lot of value in using these Charms (and their prereqs) to play the double-agent (hence why I\u2019m in the process of working up a second persona for Knight Raiton when I want to engage in shadier behavior).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, being a double agent is just the person's cover story so that none of the groups will to heavily question why the person is clearly meeting with rivals. Their actual purpose is far more sinister.<br /> <br /> Being a meeting point between various seemingly irreconcilable factions with the ultimate purpose of bringing them together as a force of mutual cooperation, by means of having each convinced that the Solar is not only in favour of their particular views and agenda, and is manipulating the others to fall in line with it!<br /> <br /> WoooOoohhh {spooky hand waving}<br /> <br /> I think the big thing about the time it takes to switch personas is that it prevents somebody from changing their Intimacies on the fly in a manner that turns it into a perfect defence against social influence.<br /> <br /> I think the point is that you're supposed to spend some time scouting out a social situation and deciding ahead of time what configuration of Intimacies will be suitable for heading into it. If you expect to be seduced and manipulated, you ought to spare the time to adopt a mindset that will effectively weather such overtures.<br /> <br /> If you don't expect to be seduced and go about with passions and priorities that leave you susceptible to such appeals... Yes, obviously you should be vulnerable to them. Why on Earth wouldn't you be?<br /> <br /> It certainly sounds to me like the statement of &quot;you should be able to change personas immediately, lest somebody catch you out by seducing you&quot; becomes a lot worse when one of those words is substituted for &quot;persuade at all&quot;, which seduction is really just a very narrow subset of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T22:33:47-07:00","id":1335988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335514#post1335514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's look at how other splats approach the idea of becoming someone else!</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars should be a really fun one for this!<br /> <br /> I have to wonder why Terrifying Forest-Devil Mask wasn't in it for DBs though, are you just doing socialize style stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T02:27:05-07:00","id":1336006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335988#post1335988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars should be a really fun one for this!<br /> <br /> I have to wonder why Terrifying Forest-Devil Mask wasn't in it for DBs though, are you just doing socialize style stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Socialize is where a lot of it is, so missing some charms in other abilities that belong to a splat he isn't playing seems easy enough to do by mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T03:43:29-07:00","id":1336012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e?p=1335961#post1335961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no, being a double agent is just the person's cover story...</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say &quot;<i>be</i> a double agent.&quot; I said &quot;<i>play</i> the double-agent.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0